-- The expected grants of every table, view, column and function in schemas
-- public, app and internal. 03_privileges.sql includes this file and compares
-- it to the live catalog (AD-3 "locked by default", P0-006). This file is not
-- run as a test itself.
--
-- Update it in the same change as the migration that adds or changes a table,
-- column, function or view. List every object, even one with no grants.
--
-- One line per object: kind|object|grants
--   kind     table, view, materialized view, foreign table, column, function
--            (also aggregates and window functions) or procedure
--   object   schema.name, schema.table.column, or schema.name(identity args)
--            for a function, as pg_get_function_identity_arguments prints them
--   grants   space-separated grantee:PRIV,PRIV; grantee PUBLIC for everyone;
--            PRIV* when grantable; ALL when a table or view grantee holds every
--            privilege; empty for no grants. Order does not matter.
--   The object's owner and extension-owned objects are left out. Every column
--   of every table and view has its own line; its grants are column-level
--   grants only (table-level grants sit on the table line), so most are empty.
--
-- Examples:
--   table|app.classes|authenticated:SELECT service_role:ALL
--   column|app.classes.name|authenticated:UPDATE
--   function|internal.add_student_as(actor uuid, student uuid)|
--
-- Reading a failure: tests 1 (object missing here) and 2 (stale line) print
-- fixture lines; the other tests do not. pgTAP prints each row as record text:
-- in parentheses, and when the line holds a space, a parenthesis or a double
-- quote also inside double quotes with every inner " doubled, e.g.
--   (column|app.t.id|)
--   ("function|public.f()|PUBLIC:EXECUTE anon:EXECUTE")
--   ("table|app.""order""|")
-- Paste the text inside the parentheses, dropping the outer double quotes and
-- turning each "" back into ". For a missing object, paste it below after
-- checking its grants are what you intend. For a stale line, delete it. Test 3
-- prints the object with the expected and actual grants. Test 4 prints one
-- grant to anon or PUBLIC per row, and tests 5 and 6 print only the object
-- name. Tests 4, 5 and 6 fail whatever this file says.
copy pg_temp.privilege_fixture (kind, object, grants) from stdin with (format csv, delimiter '|', quote e'\x01', header true);
kind|object|grants
table|internal.job_failures|
column|internal.job_failures.id|
column|internal.job_failures.job|
column|internal.job_failures.error_code|
column|internal.job_failures.detail|
column|internal.job_failures.failed_at|
column|internal.job_failures.reported_at|
table|internal.job_health_checks|
column|internal.job_health_checks.checked_at|
function|public.job_health(run_at timestamp with time zone)|service_role:EXECUTE
\.
